When it becomes too difficult to move shrubs apart with your hands, you take long hand-made machete out of your bag, like in comic books. You made it with your dad, just for fun. Father kept grumbling, that such knife is not a toy for kids. Probably, now he would be glad for you. You imagine yourself an adventurer, who goes through the jungle for treasure. 
Your efforts turn out well, and soon through gaps between bushes you see the lake, that you are heading for.  
Finally, last bushes fall under your pressure, and with a sense of relief you step on the silty shore of the lake, leaving thick shrubberies behind.